+# Owned 12306 QA helper R1 — build-only candidate
 
-This is a new self-instrumentation package, `org.droidloom.qa.amazon.r1`, derived from the retained Bilibili R5 build02 source. It never instruments Amazon's process. Its only commercial target is `com.amazon.mShop.android.shopping`, Android user 0, actual UID 10129, on the retained Main epoch. Existing Bilibili helpers and the old v2 helper are unchanged.
+This new self-instrumented package is org.droidloom.qa.ticket.r1. It targets only the currently observed com.MobileTicket UID 10121 on user/display 0 and the pinned Main epoch. Its manifest contains no permissions, activity, service, provider, receiver, debugger or commercial instrumentation target. Actual installation, signer, APK bytes and a new helper UID must be bound after the separate real build. It neither replaces an existing helper nor inherits another app's Android qualification.
 
-## Scope and unchanged mechanism
+The source derives from the actual-built Amazon R1 helper. Exact package/UID/protocol/activity-regex/resource-regex/signing label/source/output literals are changed; the current owned UiAutomation connection, public cache-clear requirement, focused application/display/type/package gates, complete tree/limits, fresh action validation, state restoration and independent after-state remain. The SDK31 compile jar, min31/target33, pinned JDK21/aapt/D8/zipalign/apksigner and 1 CPU/512 MiB/swap0/128-task budget are unchanged.
 
-The Java and Python wire contracts retain the R5 public `UiAutomation.clearCache()` check before every window query, focused application window on display 0, exact package/UID, complete tree and window hashes, fresh selected node, and one acknowledged action per nonce. Reflection accesses the public no-argument method because compilation uses the pinned SDK 31 public jar; runtime API 34 or newer and an actual `true` result are required. There is no hidden API or fallback.
+This first 12306 revision admits only state, inspect and one source-bound ACTION_CLICK. Java rejects every other operation before nonce claim or UiAutomation connection; Python request and plan entries also reject it. The inherited set_text implementation and old query constant remain unreachable, deliberately retaining the proven body instead of guessing a 12306 query or selector. No text, touch, Back, purchase, booking, login, account mutation, permission grant, setting write or audio operation is admitted. Any eventual click must be individually scoped by a reviewed caller and a fresh complete inspection; this build request does not grant UI authority.
 
-The 2-second window availability deadline, 100 ms bounded recheck, 64 query cap, 8-second work deadline, 12-second watchdog, 512 nodes, depth 32, 512 KiB result and existing independent restoration checks are unchanged. A `state` request never obtains a UiAutomation connection. UI operations use `FLAG_DONT_SUPPRESS_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICES`; no shell permission adoption, setting writes, permission grants, touch exploration, network permission, Activity, service or receiver is added.
+The retained read-only current evidence establishes UID 10121/version275, one exact APK and launcher com.MobileTicket/.ui.activity.WelcomeGuideActivity. That launcher is historical metadata only and must be resolved again immediately before a future owned launch. It does not establish a current screen or selector. The eventual host adapter must validate the single target APK, this new helper's actual signed APK and UID, hold Main namespace/root bindings, take the action lock, and preserve original exact-task cleanup. The inherited standalone adapter remains intentionally denied until that target-specific adapter exists.
 
-`set_text` accepts only the fixed public query `usb c cable`. It requires a fresh observed Amazon resource ID, an enabled visible non-password EditText supporting `ACTION_SET_TEXT`, the exact inspected node and full tree, and actual value readback. No Amazon search resource ID or current screen has been guessed. The future host plan must select a unique control from a new actual inspection; this build does not authorize a click or set-text plan.
